From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:40:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: handle ThinkSmart stock firmware init and bufferless EOS

The ThinkSmart View's stock Venus firmware counts adjacent codec-support
and max-session records as one system-init property and leaves padding
and an incomplete capability beyond the advertised count. Validate the
pair, stop at that count, and report trailing bytes. Bound variable
records by the wire payload, using field offsets for raw formats with
trailing plane records.

The firmware may signal decoder EOS with no buffer address or with a
tag that no longer names a queued CAPTURE buffer. Intercept addressless
EOS before lookup so dummy tag zero is never mistaken for buffer zero.
For a missing tag on a nonzero address, accept only a successful, empty
client-visible CAPTURE completion, excluding corrupt or dropped frames
and internal DPB returns. Limit both firmware quirks to the ThinkSmart
View's MSM8953 Venus instance.

Complete bufferless EOS once, outside the HFI IRQ thread, on a queued
CAPTURE buffer not owned by firmware. If none is eligible, defer LAST
and the EOS event until CAPTURE is queued. Track firmware ownership
separately from delayed submission eligibility, and clear the latter
when returning or flushing buffers so they cannot be submitted again
after a resolution change, STREAMOFF, or restart.

Publish the drain state before sending EOS or continuing after CAPTURE
reconfiguration, so a fast LAST completion sees the correct state.
Hold a runtime PM reference while sending STOP, and restore the
previous state if command submission or CAPTURE setup fails.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View integration
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/0787d11dd876882fdbe751781dea9dbe5bd69153
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/e91150ba18ed3d970c28c28a50290d1ebd9c9ac2
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/e82e06f1b6539c488fd060e53138d1216b79fc9f
Reference: https://github.com/jethac/lenovo-thinksmart-view/blob/fe9c0a58a1a2b7c4893f2ff76ff5c0b90206d458/kernel/patches/0703-media-venus-vdec-deliver-an-EOS-the-firmware-signals-on-a-returned-buffer.patch
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
